# Diagnostics
lint/banUncommittedTransaction  FIXABLE  ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

  × Transaction is never committed or rolled back.
  
  i Postgres rolls back the open transaction when the session ends, so its changes are not applied.
  
  i Add a COMMIT or ROLLBACK statement to complete the transaction.
  


## Fix (unsafe): Add COMMIT at the end
```
-- The file ends without a semicolon and uses psql variables. The fix adds the missing
-- semicolon before the COMMIT, and it is checked on the text of the file with the variables
-- read as parameters.
-- expect_lint/banUncommittedTransaction
begin;
create table :"schema".users (id bigint default :'id');
commit;
```
